it's the whole thing is so trippy to me  and so excited  it's really it's really bananas  catherine hahn has a spellbound with her  role on wandavision  while she's no newcomer to the acting  scene her role as agatha harkness breaks  the mold of her previous work  a magical performance like that takes a  ton of work from makeup to wardrobe to  hand gestures  and brushing up on mcu's lore star of  the show  han really threw her all into bringing  agatha and agnes to life on screen  this is gonna be a gas  catherine han came to the set with her  own ideas about the makeup for the 80s  era of episode four  featuring bright pink lipstick and heavy  purple eyeliner that gave her a look  straight out of an old 80s aerobics  video similar to the look agnes rocks in  the episode  han did have a perm back in the day she  only got one though so  she ended up with straight hair on top  and fried perm hair on the bottom as it  grew out  luckily no one on set was required to  get perms switching between the wildly  different hairstyles of the decades  wasn't practical for filming  or healthy hair wandavision scenes were  filmed out of order and sometimes they  worked on more than one era in a single  day  the solution was providing wigs for each  decade from the 50s to the 80s  for all of the show's principal actors  there's no shortage of praise from the  team behind the costumes in one division  especially from catherine herself she  called costume designer mayas rubeo a  wizard as she marveled at her attention  to detail  the designer is such a genius and such  an artist every little thing was era  appropriate  even the undergarments wearing  everything from corseted dresses  to pants with naughty bedazzled on the  butt catherine rocked  every look she wore on the show her  favorite costume was her getup for the  50s  she recalled rubeo choosing each color  carefully according to what would pop  the most in the black and white footage  her only regret is that the audience  didn't get to see the colorful clothes  in all their glory  hopefully we'll get to see all those  sets and costumes in full color when the  making of wandavision comes out  the hand gestures for spell casting in  the mcu look so cool because they're  carefully choreographed  if preparing for the role of agatha  harkness was anything like benedict  cumberbatch's training to play doctor  strange  she probably worked with a hand  choreographer cumberbatch worked with  breakdancer jay funk  who designed each gesture and movement  for the sorcerer supreme's magic  it takes a lot of practice to get the  movements just right when han would  practice her hand gestures at home  much to her kids embarrassment it was as  if they had walked in on me just getting  out of the shower they literally were  like oh my god mom  like i was practicing my witch moves and  they were so embarrassed  she thinks they were impressed with the  final product with the special effects  your own teenagers are probably the  hardest critics to impress so  that practice paid off  jumping into the mcu with no prior  knowledge is a daunting task  like diving right into the deep end of a  pool that was exactly what catherine han  did when she accepted the role of agatha  harkness  despite providing the voice of dr olivia  octavia and into the spider-verse  she wasn't all that well-versed in the  lore of the live-action marvel movies  she had a lot of research to do not only  reading the comics to learn about agatha  but  familiarizing herself with the entirety  of the mcu  it was a little bit of a word salad  walking into this i i couldn't remember  who was who and what was what luckily  she had some help  her kids were able to help her make  sense of everything going on in the  marvel movies  with the success of wandavision and the  big reveal of agatha harkness  catherine hahn has absolutely stolen the  show in what has been termed the hana  songs  she's getting some well-deserved  recognition gifts and memes of agnes and  agatha have been all over social media  bringing catherine han into the  spotlight it's a testament to how her  performance has really charmed us  but this isn't the first time we've seen  han stealing the spotlight  really she's been putting on amazing  performances and stealing  any scene she's in for years oh your  life is gross  my life is amazing now her status as a  household name has taken off with the  success of wandavision  we all know that the best villains have  their own song after being released as  part of the one division soundtrack on  february 23rd  agatha all along rocketed up to the  number one spot on itunes with more than  two million streams and counting on  spotify  han's reaction she was baffled catherine  doesn't use social media so the news  came as a huge shock to her  like i don't have social media so the  whole thing was like filtered down  through like all this i was like  are you kidding me she expressed her  amazement at the massive fan response in  an interview with seth meyers  laughing in disbelief and calling the  song success bonkers  i was told i was also like  what the success of agatha all along is  hardly surprising to us though  considering it was brought to us by the  same songwriting duo that worked on  frozen two  that explains why none of us have been  able to get that jaunty little jingle  out of our heads  marvel is infamous for its tight-lipped  policies when it comes to keeping plot  details from their actors  but not for katherine han it seems when  she met with marvel executives they laid  out the entire plot of wandavision for  her  since it was critical that she  understood her role as agatha harkness  even while playing agnes i am  really turning out to be a fantastic  secret keeper despite marvel's penchant  for secrecy  she ended up spilling a few details to  her kids but given that most of her work  is too mature for them to enjoy  she probably couldn't help herself she  was excited to be able to share one of  her acting roles with them and watching  one division together became a friday  night ritual for her family  just be able to like watch it with them  has been such a sweet  friday night ritual that i'm gonna be  i'm already nostalgic  the casting process for marvel studios  is long and involved  so long that tom holland initially  thought he hadn't landed the role of  spider-man  at all after going months without  hearing back from marvel's executives  for katherine han though the process was  unusually fast  it seems like her character isn't the  only one breaking all the rules  han happened to visit for an unrelated  general meeting with luis desposito  around the same time the writers sat  down to think about who they wanted to  play agnes  immediately someone brought up catherine  general meetings are already pretty rare  for marvel studios  the fact that it coincided so closely  with the casting meeting for agatha is  timing  so perfect it almost seems like fate we  don't usually cast like that  it's not usually like who came in the  other day let's cast them  it's almost never like that as a matter  of fact but it's usually never as  perfect as this  said kevin feige  what was it that drew catherine han to  the role if she wasn't already a big fan  of the mcu  according to her it was an acting  challenge she couldn't resist  she loved the idea of playing a single  character through the lens of different  decades  evolving to fit each era while remaining  true to the character's core  there was also a huge appeal in playing  a powerful witch hiding in plain sight  i couldn't have dreamt a cooler part  honestly i was thrilled she gushed  watching her in the role it's easy to  see that she's having tons of fun with  it  don't shoot i'm just a messenger  with a resume like hers it's no wonder  catherine hahn absolutely nails it as  the hilariously nosy neighbor agnes  as well as the manipulative magic user  agatha she's finally being recognized as  an underappreciated talent and despite  rarely landing a starring role she's  been stealing the show as supporting  cast and side characters for years  she has a strong comedic background from  her roles in shows and movies like parks  and rec  i love dick and bad moms but she's fully  capable of drama too  she shows off her acting chops and i  know this much is true  and private life not to mention into the  spider-verse where she proved that  she has what it takes to pull off an  iconic chaotic marvel villain  my enemies call me doc ock she's a  skilled performer that always  brings charisma to the table and it's  about time she got some recognition for  it  as if we didn't already have enough  reasons to love catherine hahn  her family has been fostering kittens  from a local animal shelter during the  pandemic  it was her daughter's idea but she's  loved the experience of offering their  home to animals in need during a time of  crisis
 

